<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Atomberg – FLOW 2 ONLY  (long-press a device tile → "Share device")
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Runs ONLY DeviceShareLongPressFlowTest, i.e. the flow:

      ADMIN : Home → long-press device tile → "Share device"
              → "Share access to family?" dialog → Yes
              → QR + invite code → read code into a variable
      MEMBER: More → Manage family → (+) Add → enter code → Join
              → Home → Switch Family → the admin's family
      VERIFY: both phones list the SAME devices
      CLEANUP: member leaves family + admin removes member

  Permission levels (Super / Basic / Custom) are ON HOLD — the feature is not in
  production yet and the long-press path presents no picker on the current build.
  The access matrix stays in SharedAccess/PermissionModel for when the APK that
  exposes the levels is installed on both phones.

  Use this suite when you do NOT want the Flow-1 (Manage Family → FAB → QR)
  tests to run. The full suite — which also includes DeviceSharingFlowTest
  (Flow 1), FanUiControlPermissionTest and SharingEdgeCaseTest, all of which
  share via the Manage Family path — stays in testng-sharing.xml.

  ── Run ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      mvn test "-DsuiteFile=testng-flow2.xml"

  Both phones must be connected, pre-logged-in (admin on ADMIN_DEVICE_UDID,
  member on MEMBER_DEVICE_UDID) and the admin's family must already contain the
  fan, lock and water purifier named in sharing-test.properties.
  Listeners are registered once via @Listeners on BaseDeviceSharingTest.
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<suite name="Atomberg – Device Sharing Flow 2 (long-press)" verbose="2">

    <test name="Flow 2 – long-press share (two phones)">
        <classes>
            <class name="com.appTest.tests.DeviceShareLongPressFlowTest"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

</suite>
